<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria 9-mth coupon T-bills only 4.0 pct sold.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria 9-mth coupon T-bills only 4.0 pct sold.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry 3.0 billion lev issue of nine-month floater coupon T-bills, dated September 18, was only four percent sold, yielding 255.55 percent, the Bulgarian National Bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with no minimum acceptable price set in advance by the ministry and a coupon equal to the BNB's central interest rate was for the period to maturity. The CIR is now set at 108 percent annually.</p>
<p>Four financial instituitions took part in Monday's auction, the BNB said in a statement.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices are in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		BG 3017996029</p>
<p> Type			  Floater coupon</p>
<p> Par value		   3.0 bln levs</p>
<p> Auction date		Sept 16, 1996</p>
<p> Issue date		  Sept 18, 1996</p>
<p> Maturity date	     June 18, 1997</p>
<p> Bids received	     738 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	 65.16 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved	     120 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	70.00 levs</p>
<p> Yield to maturity	 158.25 pct</p>
<p>Cumulative annual yield 255.55 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
</text>
